cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use agentcourier in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "agentcourier: encrypted messages and files between AI agents across machines"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hermann
    given-names: Alexander
version: 2.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-07
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/alhermann/agentcourier"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/agentcourier/"
abstract: >-
  agentcourier is an MCP server that lets AI coding agents such as Claude Code,
  Codex and GitHub Copilot exchange messages and files across machines, for
  example between a laptop and an HPC cluster. Machines are paired once;
  every connection is end-to-end encrypted with a post-quantum hybrid key exchange.
keywords:
  - model context protocol
  - AI agents
  - agent-to-agent communication
  - HPC
  - end-to-end encryption
